Let Λ = {λ_n}_{n∈ℕ} be a sequence of pairwise distinct complex numbers with 0 ∉ Λ and |λ_n| → ∞ as n → ∞. Define the exponential system Exp Λ = {e^{λ_n z} : n ∈ ℕ}. For a set X ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ (viewed as a subset of the complex plane), let H(X) denote the space of continuous complex-valued functions on X that are holomorphic in the interior of X (when the interior is nonempty), equipped with the topology of uniform convergence on compact subsets of X. The system Exp Λ is said to be complete in H(X) if the closed linear span of Exp Λ in H(X) equals H(X).

Characterize, in terms of Λ, when Exp Λ is complete in H(X) in each of the following cases:
(i) X = (−a, a) for some a ∈ (0, +∞];
(ii) X = [0, +∞);
(iii) X = (−∞, 0].

